ion so protected endpoints accept either a Bearer access token or an authenticated session cookie, letting API clients and browser/admin sessions share one endpoint surface."}, {"id": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_token_storage_guidance", "label": "Client Token Storage Guidance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "backend/AUTH_JWT_DRAFT.md", "source_location": "Frontend instructions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tokens should be held in memory or secure storage and localStorage avoided because it is readable by injected script if XSS occurs; refresh tokens warrant stricter storage than access tokens and should be rotated on logout, and access lifetimes kept short for sensitive flows."}, {"id": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_optional_simplejwt", "label": "Optional SimpleJWT Degradation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "backend/AUTH_JWT_DRAFT.md", "source_location": "Notes / Requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registration still succeeds when djangorestframework-simplejwt is absent, but returns no tokens - the token issuance path is conditional on the library being installed rather than a hard dependency of the register flow."}], "edges": [{"source": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_register_endpoint", "target": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_registerview", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/AUTH_JWT_DRAFT.md", "source_location": "How it works (backend)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_registerview", "target": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_registerserializer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/AUTH_JWT_DRAFT.md", "source_location": "How it works (backend)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "backend_auth_jwt_draft_registerview", "target": "backend_requirements_simplejwt", "relation": "references", "confidenc